d <ei15 issuance> of nearly 1.8 million common shares in connection with the land purchase will <ei16 bring> MGM Grand 's total shares outstanding to 28.7 million , of which 72 % will be <ei17 owned> by Mr. Kerkorian and Tracinda , <ei18 according> to the prospectus . In over-the-counter <ei19 trading> , MGM Grand was <ei20 bid> at $ 17.50 a share . Proceeds from the offering are <ei21 expected> to be <ei22 used> for <ei23 remodeling> the company 's Desert Inn resort in Las Vegas , <ei24 refurbishing> certain aircraft of the MGM Grand Air unit , and to <ei25 acquire> the property for the new resort . The company <ei26 said> it <ei27 estimates> the Desert Inn remodeling will <ei28 cost> about $ 32 million , and the <ei29 refurbishment> of the three DC-8-62 aircraft , made by McDonnell Douglas Corp., will <ei30 cost> around $ 24.5 million . MGM Grand <ei31 said> the latest stock offering wo n't <ei32 cover> the $ 600 million or more cost of <ei33 building> the proposed resort and theme park , and <ei34 added> it will <ei35 need> to <ei36 seek> additional financing , either through bank borrowings or debt and equity offerings , at a later date . <ei38 Construction> is <ei39 set> to <ei40 begin> in early 1991 . The resort will include the MGM Grand Hotel , a multi-spired , castle-like facility that will include 5,000 rooms and 85,000 square feet of casino space . The facility will be <ei42 marketed> toward families , and room rates will be between $ 35 and $ 55 a night , MGM Grand <ei43 said> . The prospectus did n't <ei44 include> many details about the studio and theme park , although conceptual drawings , <ei45 released> this month , <ei47 show> that it may <ei48 feature> several \" themed \" areas similar to those found at parks built by Walt Disney Co.", "gold": [], "lang": "eng", "mentions": ["ei1", "ei2", "ei3", "ei4", "ei5", "ei6", "ei7", "ei8", "ei10", "ei11", "ei12", "ei13", "ei14", "ei15", "ei16", "ei17", "ei18", "ei19", "ei20", "ei21", "ei22", "ei23", "ei24"